# Wave W17-P (Route 119): gauge box — a Weather Institute rain-gauge box on its post: a lidded instrument box with a pale funnel at its head and fine measurement lines ruled down its face, logging every drop that falls on this route (design: the Institute keeps the ledgers; its gauge boxes stand along the rain road like small patient clerks). On gauge turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from Route 118’s hand-cut ford posts by instrument: the river’s gauge is read by eye, the Institute’s by ledger.
